    "title": "Check Your Understanding",
    "long_instructions": "A designer on another team at the studio has a classifier that tags items in a game as “common” or “rare” from three numbers: what level it was found in, how many enemies guarded the item, and how long the player took to reach it. It currently runs on `n_neighbors = 1`.\r\n- Which numbers in that program are hyperparameters, and which are features? How can you tell the two apart?\r\n- Describe, step by step, how you would tune this classifier, and how you would know which setting to tell the designer to choose.\r\n",
